[[0,1265604,0,1,0,1,"2016-09-02T16:53:18","ChillyHellion","",[],"","The Steam Hardware Survey for August 2016 shows Linux has grown again","https://www.gamingonlinux.com/articles/the-steam-hardware-survey-for-august-2016-shows-linux-has-grown-again.7986","gaming"],[1,6225129,0,1,0,1,"2016-09-02T16:53:31","ChillyHellion","",[],"<p>x-post <a href=\"/v/coopgaming\">/v/CoOpGaming</a> :: <a href=\"https://archive.is/UwDt2\">Archive</a></p>"],[1,6225955,0,2,0,2,"2016-09-02T18:34:23","zaqu","",[],"<p>I'd switch tomorrow if there was decent support , heck , if within two years they could properly support my everything currently on the store i would switch. They could charge 40$ for the GAMEoS(linux dedicated game os) and within 5 years it could have a visible market-share , people like paying money for things </p>"],[1,6228202,0,2,0,2,"2016-09-03T00:19:13","Codewow","",[],"<p>Grown, but not without growing pains.</p>"],[2,6228251,6228202,2,0,2,"2016-09-03T00:25:20","ChillyHellion","",[],"<p>That's true, and the amount grown is still very small percentages. What's most interesting to me is that most of the recent growth seems to have come at the expense of Apple's marketshare instead of Microsoft's. I know most people on Voat want Linux to eat Windows 10's lunch, but taking Apple's place as the biggest non-Windows gaming platform is a great stepping stone towards that end. </p>"]]
